WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.220
Two-brain regions linked to memory and emotion begin shrinking up to a decade before memory loss appears in Alzheimer's. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 245. Physicians missing a drop in diagnostic AI, plant-based diet quality against obesity-related cancer, and a fiber blend for IBS come next, with a sleep-timing deep dive and a week in review after that. John's Hopkins researchers, according to Science Daily, examine hundreds of magnetic resonance imaging,

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:35.500
or MRI, and positron emission tomography, or PET scans, drawn from the Alzheimer's disease

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:40.960
neuroimaging initiative, and the biomarkers of cognitive decline among normal individual

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.420
study.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:47.100
The antoreonal cortex and the amygdala showed greater tissue loss than the hippocampus during

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.540
early stages, and those structural changes overlapped with areas of abnormal tau-protein

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:56.260
accumulation detected by PET imaging and digital pathology.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:01.940
The pattern held across participants without symptoms, those with cognitive impairment and

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:03.560
patients who died from the disease.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:09.240
The antoreonal cortex helps retrieve previously stored memories while the amygdala contributes

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.480
to emotional memory, and senior author Michael Miller worked with co-author Marilyn Albert,

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.400
who stated the goal is to treat individuals before symptoms develop.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:24.340
The findings were published in neuroimage reports and presented at Neuroscience 2026.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:24.440
6.

00:01:25.397 --> 00:01:30.737
Medical students and physicians in a controlled test reported via science subreddit used an

00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:36.137
artificial intelligence or AI diagnostic system whose accuracy researchers had deliberately

00:01:36.137 --> 00:01:36.657
lowered.

00:01:37.237 --> 00:01:42.857
48 people sat with that degraded system, and only 12.5% of them noticed the drop.

00:01:43.357 --> 00:01:48.777
When participants first made their own diagnoses and then saw the AI recommendations, they're

00:01:48.777 --> 00:01:52.217
in their own diagnoses declined faster than their trust in the AI.

00:01:52.217 --> 00:01:57.865
high. Healthy plant-based eating was tracked against obesity-related cancers in a 13-year

00:01:57.865 --> 00:02:06.165
follow-up of 16,256 adults. A healthy plant-based diet was linked to 33% lower risk. Overall,

00:02:06.405 --> 00:02:11.405
plant-based diets showed no association with that risk, and unhealthy plant-based diets showed

00:02:11.405 --> 00:02:17.522
none either. A specially designed fiber blend, according to Science Daily, was tested in people

00:02:17.522 --> 00:02:22.102
with irritable bowel syndrome, or IBS, and reduced gut-related anxiety.

00:02:22.802 --> 00:02:26.282
The same blend produced rapid shifts in gut bacteria composition.

00:02:27.002 --> 00:02:32.162
Bloating did not worsen, pain did not worsen, and other digestive symptoms did not worsen.

00:02:33.201 --> 00:02:37.801
University of Missouri researchers tracked older adults who kept regular times for sleeping,

00:02:38.161 --> 00:02:39.481
eating, and other activities.

00:02:40.161 --> 00:02:43.241
People with consistent schedules reported lower physical pain.

00:02:43.241 --> 00:02:48.721
They also reported fewer depressive symptoms even when insomnia was present, and the

00:02:48.721 --> 00:02:53.321
pattern suggests the body's internal clock influences both mood and physical comfort.

00:02:54.409 --> 00:02:59.769
Young adults in a four-month supervised rehabilitation program after anterior cruciate ligament

00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:05.049
or ACL, reconstruction improved on pain, muscle strength, and quality of life.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:10.549
Cartilage measurements showed no additional damage from the exercise. The results challenge

00:03:10.549 --> 00:03:13.449
concerns that early loading worsens joint outcomes.

00:03:14.442 --> 00:03:19.222
Chemical signatures and fossilized dinosaur teeth revealed intake of nutrients from seaweed

00:03:19.222 --> 00:03:22.642
and other ocean sources more than 100 million years ago.

00:03:23.262 --> 00:03:28.062
Those marine resources moved through ancient food chains to herbivores living near coasts.

00:03:28.582 --> 00:03:30.962
Predators living near coasts received them as well.

00:03:31.982 --> 00:03:37.822
Wild female Asian elephants in Sri Lanka, in a 12-year study of more than 440 animals

00:03:37.822 --> 00:03:42.982
discussed via science subreddit, showed social connections changing before head counts did.

00:03:43.602 --> 00:03:48.882
Large interconnected communities broke into smaller isolated groups ahead of measurable population

00:03:48.882 --> 00:03:54.682
drops. That fragmentation could reduce cooperation within herds, and it could reduce information

00:03:54.682 --> 00:04:01.976
sharing as well. Climate distress in a United States study of people aged 13-22 can spur environmental

00:04:01.976 --> 00:04:07.236
action. Participants who felt annoyed by climate messaging were more likely to disengage.

00:04:07.236 --> 00:04:10.856
That disengagement pattern was labeled equal paralysis.

00:04:11.947 --> 00:04:15.427
Routine heart scans run through AI, according to Science Daily,

00:04:15.967 --> 00:04:18.567
revealed a previously unrecognized warning pattern.

00:04:18.827 --> 00:04:21.687
The signal outperformed conventional screening methods

00:04:21.687 --> 00:04:24.487
for identifying people at risk of fatal heart malfunction.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.220
Mild cognitive impairment cases in data-driven subtyping

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:31.060
reported via science subreddit,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.500
resolved into four separate trajectories of cognitive change.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:39.380
The approach used longitudinal measures to separate groups that follow different paths

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:45.615
toward dementia or toward stability. Peptides derived from a sleep-related protein in fruit

00:04:45.615 --> 00:04:51.175
flies cause ribosomes in resistant bacteria to clump. That clumping disrupted bacterial

00:04:51.175 --> 00:04:57.556
protein synthesis. The mechanism did not rely on conventional antibiotic targets. In

00:04:57.556 --> 00:05:03.156
brief, Australian doctors, according to ABC News, link rising health anxiety to social

00:05:03.156 --> 00:05:08.116
media algorithms and longevity marketing. With general practitioners reporting that roughly

00:05:08.116 --> 00:05:13.256
half their patients now discuss health worries, triggered by online content promoting predictive

00:05:13.256 --> 00:05:18.516
tests and supplements, algorithms amplifying fears and leading some to undergo unneeded

00:05:18.516 --> 00:05:24.916
scans at high cost. Genomic analysis mapped a dominant microplasma-toda species, colonizing

00:05:24.916 --> 00:05:31.016
the body wall of deep-sea sea cucumbers, or holothorians, and traced its spatial distribution

00:05:31.016 --> 00:05:33.976
and evolutionary adaptations to the host environment.

00:05:34.858 --> 00:05:38.058
Most people assume that the total hours spent a sleep each night

00:05:38.058 --> 00:05:42.498
determine cardiovascular risk when the heart appears to register something else,

00:05:42.978 --> 00:05:44.878
how steadily sleep lands on the clock.

00:05:45.558 --> 00:05:48.758
Consistency of when sleep occurs appears to carry greater weight

00:05:48.758 --> 00:05:50.798
than how long the night lasts on average.

00:05:51.318 --> 00:05:55.898
A study of 10,362 adults measured both average sleep duration

00:05:55.898 --> 00:05:59.378
and night-to-night timing regularity over extended periods.

00:05:59.378 --> 00:06:05.078
Irregular sleep schedules correlated with a 24% higher cardiovascular event rate.

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:07.898
Average duration showed no significant link.

00:06:08.458 --> 00:06:13.218
The same data indicated that more stable sleep cycles also tracked with lower arrhythmia

00:06:13.218 --> 00:06:13.738
incidents.

00:06:14.318 --> 00:06:18.938
The body's internal timing system influences heart rhythm stability through daily alignment

00:06:18.938 --> 00:06:21.518
of metabolic signals and autonomic signals.

00:06:22.218 --> 00:06:27.158
Bedtime and wake time can be anchored within a 30-minute window on most days, with morning

00:06:27.158 --> 00:06:32.958
energy or resting heart rate tracked against that window. After today's look at early brain change,

00:06:33.238 --> 00:06:38.458
daily clocks, and what the heart registers in sleep timing, the past seven days also ran through

00:06:38.458 --> 00:06:44.078
rock, ice, and the price of carbon. Tiny crystals in Andean volcanic rocks share a chemical

00:06:44.078 --> 00:06:49.778
signature tied to hot magma intrusions that destabilized shallow reservoirs before eruptions.

00:06:50.578 --> 00:06:56.158
Arctic ice cores show Montana mining sent heavy metals across continents in the late 1800s.

00:06:56.158 --> 00:07:02.278
A model shows land-based climate measures can achieve 1.7 degrees Celsius targets with

00:07:02.278 --> 00:07:06.298
a carbon price of $180 per ton instead of $400.

00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:12.358
Before we go, trials that deliberately stabilize sleep timing and then measure cardiac markers

00:07:12.358 --> 00:07:17.758
are the longer-term test of whether clock alignment, not hours in bed, is what the heart

00:07:17.758 --> 00:07:18.518
responds to.

